@title STORY • RILEY: NO RULES
@bg lake_dock_night
You're Riley Bennett. Winger. Nashville. You're on a dock at 2 a.m., barefoot, because you can be.
@show nia
Nia: (walking up) You're gonna fall in.
Riley: Then I'll swim.
Nia: It's October. You'll freeze.
Riley: Then I'll be a cool ghost.
You've been best friends since you were nine. She's always the one telling you to get down.
> [Bitchy] "Why do you always have to ruin everything, Nia?" -> a1
> [Sweet] Grab her hand. Pull her onto the dock with you. -> a2
*a1
Nia: (quiet) I'm not trying to ruin it. I'm trying to make sure you're still around to have fun tomorrow.
You don't have anything to say to that.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Nia_Bond 3
She almost says no. Then she sits. Two girls on a dock, feet in freezing water, laughing at nothing until the sun comes up.
*a_done
@bg dorm_room_day
You know something you're not supposed to know. Nia told you in August that she liked Tyler. And you went to his house anyway.
> [Good] Tell Nia you're sorry. Today. -> b1
> [Bad] Pretend it's fine. Maybe she forgot. -> b2
*b1
@add Nia_Bond 3
Riley: I knew you liked him. I did it anyway. I don't even like him that much. I just... I wanted somebody to want me first, for once.
Nia: (long pause) That's the dumbest thing you've ever said.
Riley: I know.
Nia: I'm still mad.
Riley: I know.
Nia: ...Pancakes?
@jump end
*b2
She didn't forget. She never forgets anything about you. That's what makes it worse.
*end
Riley Bennett lives with no rules. This year, she learns that the one person who keeps telling her to get down is the one who'd jump in after her.
